Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+/3.10+):

## 1. Windows-only tests — `[OSCondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\MyApp", "Version", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI — `[CICondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void GpuShader_CompilesSuccessfully()
{
    var result = GpuCompiler.Compile("shader.hlsl");
    Assert.IsTrue(result.Success);
}
```

## 3. Flaky external API — `[Retry]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
[Timeout(10000)]
public async Task WeatherApi_ReturnsForecast(TestContext testContext)
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync(testContext.CancellationToken);
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
}
```

Use `[Retry]` only for genuinely flaky external dependencies — not to mask race conditions.

## 4. Cleanup even on failure — `[TestCleanup]`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class FileProcessingTests
{
    private string _tempFile = string.Empty;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        FileProcessor.Write(_tempFile, "data");
        Assert.AreEqual("data", File.ReadAllText(_tempFile));
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test fails or throws
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `[TestCleanup]` always runs after each test (pass or fail)
- `[OSCondition]` and `[CICondition]` require MSTest 3.10+
- `[Retry]` requires MSTest 3.9+
- Combine `[Retry]` with `[Timeout]` and `CancellationToken` for robust async tests
